---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="BOPtech platform - BOPA"
  description="BOPtech, the technology and scientific platform of the BOPA Innovation Chair, at the heart of the Hepato-Biliary Center's operating room."
>
  <section class="section-block">
    <div class="mesh-echo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap intro-split" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <span class="kicker">Innovations</span>
        <h1>BOPtech</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Funded by AP-HP, the Paris Saclay Cancer Cluster and Bpifrance,
          BOPtech is the Chair's technology and scientific platform, based
          directly inside the operating room of the Hepato-Biliary Center.
          It connects MedTech, Biotech and academic research to accelerate,
          as close to the field as possible, innovation in image-guided
          surgery, endoscopy and hepato-bilio-pancreatic oncology.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-media">
        <img
          class="intro-image"
          src="/images/boptech/foie-modele.jpg"
          alt="Anatomical liver model used for training and surgical preparation."
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-sub explainer" data-reveal>
      <h2>InMachina: how it works</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Every function of the human body is reproduced by a technical
        module, to keep an explanted liver in near-physiological
        conditions - the principle behind InMachina.
      </p>
      <img
        class="explainer-image"
        src="/images/boptech/inmachina-schema.png"
        alt="Diagram illustrating the principle of an ex vivo liver perfusion device: every function of the body is reproduced by a technical module (a pump for the heart, an oxygenator for the lungs, dialysis for the kidneys, an algorithm for control...)."
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-sub" data-reveal>
      <div class="accordion-subgrid">
        <details class="accordion-subitem" open>
          <summary>
            <span class="accordion-subtitle">InMachina: a human liver, a preclinical revolution</span>
            <svg class="accordion-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M5 7.5 10 12.5 15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="accordion-subpanel">
            <p>
              Supported by the PSCC, InMachina opens a new path in
              translational medicine: keeping cancerous human livers (HCC,
              CCA, metastases) in near-physiological conditions for 7 to 14
              days.
            </p>
            <p>
              This unique model lets biotech, medtech and healthcare
              companies test their innovations in an ultra-realistic ex vivo
              environment before any move into the clinic - to de-risk,
              validate and accelerate the development of new therapies.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="accordion-subitem" open>
          <summary>
            <span class="accordion-subtitle">Hybrid Room: the future of surgery is being built at the CHB</span>
            <svg class="accordion-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M5 7.5 10 12.5 15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="accordion-subpanel">
            <p>
              Thanks to Bpifrance's support, the CHB's Hybrid Room opens its
              doors to MedTech companies to test, validate and evolve their
              innovations under real conditions: image-guided surgery,
              endoscopy, ultrasound or interventional radiology.
            </p>
            <p>
              This platform is equipped with the <strong>Philips Azurion 7</strong>,
              a latest-generation system boosted by artificial intelligence -
              a unique opportunity to accelerate clinical development in a
              hospital environment of excellence.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-sub" data-reveal>
      <h2>Our range of services</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Innovating is good. Innovating with impact is better: draw on our
        field expertise to turn your ideas into clinical success.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Decode</h3>
          <p>Market dynamics.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Assess</h3>
          <p>The clinical acceptability of your innovations.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Optimize</h3>
          <p>The usability of your healthcare innovations.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap section-sub" data-reveal>
      <h2>Our field of excellence, your field of innovation</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        At the CHB, a reference center for liver surgery, this unique volume
        of explanted human livers offers privileged access to a living
        preclinical model, usable for several hours - a rare opportunity to
        test devices or therapies before the next stage.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .section-sub {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .intro-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .intro-image {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px -20px rgba(4, 35, 56, 0.25);
  }

  .explainer {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .explainer .lede {
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .explainer-image {
    max-width: 26rem;
    margin: var(--space-4) auto 0;
  }

  /* Accordion styling redeclared here since Astro scopes <style> blocks
     per page - index.astro's own accordion rules don't reach these same
     class names on this page. */
  .accordion-subgrid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .accordion-subitem {
    background: var(--color-bg-tint);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: box-shadow 0.25s ease;
  }

  .accordion-subitem:hover {
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(4, 35, 56, 0.06);
  }

  .accordion-subitem > summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .accordion-subitem > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .accordion-chevron {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .accordion-subitem[open] > summary .accordion-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .accordion-subpanel {
    padding: 0 var(--space-4) var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .accordion-subpanel p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .intro-split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .intro-media {
      order: -1;
    }
  }
</style>
